SUMMARY:Simple Heart: An Evening of Story & Reflection
DESCRIPTION:Simple Heart: An Evening of Story & Reflection is a thoughtfully curated literary gathering designed to invite deeper connection through story\, identity\, and shared reflection. \nThis intimate experience brings together readers and curious minds for an evening centred around a powerful true narrative and the universal question of belonging. \nThis is not your typical book event—it’s a space where stories open conversations\, and conversations lead to meaningful connection. \nThe evening offers an opportunity to reflect and engage with others in an intentional\, welcoming environment. Whether you come on your own or with someone\, you’ll be part of a room that values presence\, curiosity\, and depth. \nSpots are limited\, so reserve your ticket early. \n📍 Event Details \n\n​Date: Tuesday\, Jun 23 2026\nTime: 6:30–8:30 PM\nLocation: Reel Asian (401 Richmond St. W. Toronto\, ON.)\n\n🎟️ Your Ticket Includes \n\nEntry to an intimate\, curated event experience\nLive virtual conversation with the author from South Korea\nLight refreshments during networking\n\n🎤 Who’s Speaking \nThe evening features a live virtual conversation with Cho Haejin\, author of Simple Heart. \nBefore she was named Nana by the French couple who adopted her as a child\, she was Esther Pak\, a girl growing up in a Korean orphanage. And before she was Esther Pak\, she was Munju\, a small child abandoned on the railway tracks in Seoul. \nTogether\, we’ll explore the question at the heart of her story: What is your name?
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/simple-heart-an-evening-of-story-reflection/
LOCATION:Museum of Toronto\, 401 Richmond St W\, Toronto\, M5V 3A8
CATEGORIES:Cultural Celebrations,Literature & Spoken Word,Talks & Panels
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/simple-heart-an-evening-of-story-reflection.png
END:VEVENT
