SUMMARY:Toronto Jazz Festival presents Emilie-Claire Barlow
DESCRIPTION:Emilie-Claire Barlow is one of the most distinctive voices in Canadian jazz. A seasoned singer\, arranger and producer\, she has built an international career anchored by fourteen albums\, including La plus belle saison (to be released on February 6\, 2026)\, a heartfelt tribute to the Québec repertoire\, co-produced with pianist and arranger François Richard. The recipient of a Félix and two JUNO Awards\, Emilie-Claire Barlow has garnered over 500 million streams and performed on stages around the world. Joyful and passionate\, with a charming sense of humour\, she brings to her music a sense of playfulness\, sophistication\, a love of language\, and a voice of unforgettable beauty.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/toronto-jazz-festival-presents-emilie-claire-barlow/
LOCATION:Telus Centre For Performance And Learning\, 273 Bloor St W\, Toronto\, ON M5S 1W2\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 1W2
CATEGORIES:Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/toronto-jazz-festival-presents-emilie-claire-barlow.png
END:VEVENT
